WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
Speaker 1: Let's start today with the latest on&nbsp;
the pandemic in the United States and around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:11.200
world, then I want to look at the question Do any&nbsp;
religions actually prohibit vaccination for all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:18.880
of the talk about? I have a religious exemption&nbsp;
from being vaccinated. What religions ban being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:25.360
vaccinated? If any, we're going to look at that in&nbsp;
a moment now. Last week I came to you and I said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:32.160
COVID cases are down 53 percent in the U.S. from&nbsp;
their Delta Peak. Deaths are down 33 percent in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.760
the U.S. from their Delta Peak. That was last&nbsp;
week, and we said, what will the next week&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:44.320
look like? Well, it's now next week relative to&nbsp;
last week, and the numbers are once again better.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.320
Let's look at those numbers and see just how much&nbsp;
better the U.S. average daily COVID cases are now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:57.920
down 59 percent from their delta wave peak of&nbsp;
167 thousand a day, the U.S. now seeing 68000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:06.160
cases per day. Yes, it's a crazy number, but it's&nbsp;
the lowest it's been since late July. And for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.480
it's pointing down rather than pointing up.&nbsp;
And that's a good thing. In terms of daily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:19.280
U.S. deaths, the delta wave peak was all the way&nbsp;
back up to just a hair under 2000 deaths a day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:28.880
That is now down to about 1275 deaths a day,&nbsp;
a tragic number but a decline of 35 percent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:35.680
So both cases and deaths declining in the&nbsp;
last week. Cases declining more than deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:41.040
on a percentage basis. OK, what's the global&nbsp;
context? What's happening globally? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.960
globally, cases are actually going back up. This&nbsp;
is being led by some specific countries, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.160
I'll tell you about in a moment. But globally,&nbsp;
cases have gone up. It's not a big change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:02:00.720
but cases. Globally, we're down to about 400 3000&nbsp;
a day. They're now back up to 400 and 16000 a day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.520
It's a small change, but it could be meaningful.&nbsp;
It could mean one of two things. Number one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:12.640
we could be seeing the start of another wave with&nbsp;
winter coming to the northern hemisphere. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:19.520
a possibility. It could just be a blip. We don't&nbsp;
know yet, but this is being led by some countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.920
with major increases in cases last week. I'll&nbsp;
give you some examples. The Czech Republic has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:32.240
gone from like they were almost at zero, that&nbsp;
they had 150 cases a day. They're at 3000 a day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.880
150 to 3000 a day. That's a huge spike in the&nbsp;
Czech Republic. And when I tell you the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.160
countries where we're seeing increases, you'll&nbsp;
start to notice a regional trend. Hungary, Poland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:52.320
Slovenia are seeing big spikes. Hungary went from&nbsp;
70 cases a day to 2000. Poland went from 150 cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:03:00.400
a day to 5000. Slovenia went from 60 cases a&nbsp;
day, all the way up to about 1750. Just those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.560
few countries already. That's a major increase.&nbsp;
And you look at the others Slovakia, Croatia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:14.320
Ukraine all seeing significant increases in cases.&nbsp;
So it could be that area. Also, big concerns in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.320
the United Kingdom. At one point last week,&nbsp;
the United Kingdom had the highest case rate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:25.280
I believe in the world now, stabilizing at a very&nbsp;
bad number of 45000 cases a day in the U.K. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:31.360
all bad. So the question is, is that coming to the&nbsp;
U.K., we're coming to the U.S. Rather, we saw with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:37.440
Delta that it started in Europe and then we were&nbsp;
just lagging behind. I think it was like six to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.920
eight weeks or something like that. So is what's&nbsp;
happening in some of these European countries now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.880
going to be here in six or eight weeks? We just&nbsp;
don't know yet. You can find opinion saying yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.640
you can find opinion saying no. One view&nbsp;
is we are going to see a decline and we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.120
going to get to sort of like endemic&nbsp;
levels where you get yourself vaccinated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:04.080
If you do or participate in indoor events with a&nbsp;
bunch of people, maybe everybody gets tested. I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.040
been to a couple of events, including a birthday&nbsp;
party where that was the protocol. That's what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.840
we were getting down to that endemic level. The&nbsp;
other view is this is about to explode as we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.840
head into winter in the United States. What do&nbsp;
we know about the U.S. right now? We know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:26.720
vaccination is basically flat at a very low level.&nbsp;
We're doing about 800000 vaccinations per day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.960
with reports indicating that there&nbsp;
are more third doses in those 800k&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:39.360
than first doses. That's very, very bad. We&nbsp;
know that we are believed to be very close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.800
to vaccine approval for five to 11 year olds and&nbsp;
FDA panel recommending that approval yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.160
And now we're just waiting for broader approval.&nbsp;
It could be that we start vaccinating five to 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:57.120
year olds as soon as next Friday. That's that's&nbsp;
something we're following. We know that schools&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:02.000
where you are not required to wear. Masks are&nbsp;
seeing significantly higher COVID case rates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.400
than those where you are, so masks continue&nbsp;
to be relevant for those unvaccinated kids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:15.680
Also new The CDC is now saying that some&nbsp;
immunocompromised people can and should get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:24.000
a fourth COVID shot. That is not something that&nbsp;
was previously discussed in any great detail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:30.080
And now the CDC is saying, yeah, it's not just a&nbsp;
third dose for some immunocompromised people. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:36.000
should be looking and even starting to do fourth&nbsp;
doses. So we're going to follow all of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:43.680
cases down here. But increasing globally. And&nbsp;
the question is, are we headed for a very dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:50.080
winter or are we headed for a not so bad winter&nbsp;
with things being essentially everything open?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.840
Some places with vaccine requirements, some&nbsp;
places vaccine or testing requirements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.400
et cetera, as we've been seeing, so we will&nbsp;
continue to follow it. We'll see where we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.480
by next week. We could either be at 60 percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.040
down from the Delta Peak or we could start to&nbsp;
see a turnaround, which would not be very good.

